'''''Ptychostomum imbricatulum''''', '''handbell moss''',<ref>{{Cite GBIF|taxon=''Gemmabryum caespiticium'' (Hedw.) J.R.Spence|ID=8099233}}</ref> is a species of [[moss]] belonging to the family [[Bryaceae]].<ref name="WFO_0001214645">{{Cite WFO|genus=Ptychostomum|species=imbricatulum|authority=(Müll.Hal.) Holyoak & N.Pedersen|id=0001214355|access-date=2026-06-24}}</ref>

It has almost [[cosmopolitan distribution]].<ref name="WFO_0001214645" />

''Ptychostomum imbricatulum'' is known to be able to use [[artificial light]] to grow in places which are otherwise devoid of natural light, such as [[Crystal Cave (Wisconsin)|Crystal Cave]] in [[Wisconsin]].<ref name="Thatcher 1949">{{cite journal |last1=Thatcher |first1=Edward P. |title=Bryophytes of an Artificially Illuminated Cave |journal=The Bryologist |date=1949 |volume=52 |issue=4 |pages=212-214 |doi=10.2307/3239480 }}</ref>

